/-!
# `Work.CFT.Kummer`: Kummer theory over number fields and Shafarevich's relation-rank estimate

Aggregator for the area.  See `README.md` in this directory for the guide to the results and for
the list of what is *not* proved here (the deep arithmetic inputs, which are isolated as the named
hypotheses `Work.CFT.Kummer.UnramifiedShafarevich`, `Work.CFT.Kummer.ShafarevichTame` and
`Work.CFT.Kummer.KochTransfer`).

## Kummer theory (finite level)

* `Work.CFT.Kummer.kummer_equiv` — `(Lˣ^p ∩ Kˣ)/Kˣ^p ≃* Hom(Gal(L/K), μ_p(L))` for a finite Galois
  extension `L/K` and `μ_p ⊆ K` (Hilbert 90 + Galois descent).
* `Work.CFT.Kummer.kummer_dual_galois` — the perfect Kummer pairing: for `L/K` abelian of exponent
  dividing `p`, `Gal(L/K) ≃* Hom((Lˣ^p ∩ Kˣ)/Kˣ^p, μ_p)`.
* `Work.CFT.Kummer.kummer_adjoin_eq_top` — `L = K(ᵖ√(Lˣ^p ∩ Kˣ))`: the extension is generated by
  the Kummer generators.

## The Kummer-theoretic rank formulas

* `Work.CFT.Kummer.finrank_unitsModPow` — `dim 𝒪_Kˣ/(𝒪_Kˣ)^p = (r₁+r₂-1) + δ_{K,p}`.
* `Work.CFT.Kummer.finrank_kummerClasses_empty` — `dim V_∅/K^{×p} = dim Cl_K[p] + (r₁+r₂-1) + δ_{K,p}`.
* `Work.CFT.Kummer.finrank_kummerDual_empty` — the same for the Kummer character group `𝓒_∅`.
* `Work.CFT.Kummer.finrank_H1Fp_eq_finrank_classGroupTorsion` — the H¹ rank formula (b) at `S = ∅`
  reads `dim H¹(G_∅,𝔽_p) = dim Cl_K[p]`.

## Shafarevich's relation-rank estimate

* `Work.CFT.Kummer.finrank_H2Fp_le_H1Fp_add` — `dim H²(G_∅,𝔽_p) ≤ dim H¹(G_∅,𝔽_p) + (r₁+r₂-1) + δ`
  from facts (a) and (b) at `S = ∅`.
* `Work.CFT.Kummer.finrank_H2Fp_le_H1Fp_add_two` — the totally real cubic, `p = 3` case:
  `dim H² ≤ dim H¹ + 2`.
* `Work.CFT.Kummer.finrank_H2Fp_quotient_le_two` — the finite-quotient (Koch transfer) form.
* `Work.CFT.Kummer.finrank_H2Fp_le_kummerDual_add_card` and
  `Work.CFT.Kummer.finrank_H2Fp_add_le_H1Fp_add` — the tame `S` case with Hilbert reciprocity.
* `Work.CFT.Kummer.H2Estimate_two_of_unramifiedPresentation` — `Work.Tower.Shafarevich.H2Estimate 2`
  from the presentation data of the tower.

## The Kummer description of unramified extensions (vocabulary)

* `Work.CFT.Kummer.IsUnramifiedOutside` — `L/K` unramified at every finite place outside `S`.
* `Work.CFT.Kummer.KummerUnramifiedCorrespondence` — the named hypothesis that the Kummer
  generators of the abelian exponent-`p` extensions unramified outside `S` (and splitting at `S`)
  are exactly the classes in `V_S/K^{×p}`.
-/

